BTN0  → Emergency Alert
BTN1  → Reset
BTN2  → Optional TX trigger
BTN3  → Optional RX/ACK trigger

LD0   → System ON
LD1   → Emergency
LD2   → TX
LD3   → RX
LD4   → Packet Valid
LD5   → CRC PASS
LD6   → Forwarding
LD7   → Error


# Boolean Board UART mapping used by this prototype

The board's USB PROG/UART connector exposes the FPGA UART interface. The board schematic identifies `UART_RXD_OUT` on FPGA pin **U11** and `UART_TXD_IN` on FPGA pin **V12**. In the prototype:

- TX FPGA `uart_tx` -> V12 -> PC USB-UART receive path
- RX FPGA `uart_rx` <- U11 <- PC USB-UART transmit path
- 100 MHz clock -> F14
- BTN0 -> T5 reset
- BTN1 -> J5 emergency trigger

Use one USB cable per FPGA board if you are using two boards. Windows will normally expose two COM ports. Verify the actual COM numbers in Device Manager before running the PC bridge.
